docs/design/interactive-agent-communication-01-requirements.md:512:R-15.o [R] Ruled (OD-4 A, OD-5): STORED is the only call that releases the sender and the second step of the message states (R-44). It is written to the hub record before the call to the sender (R-45). Idempotence per stage is R-51. [R] (changed in v0.5 by CR-1, ruling 2026-10-10 A) The same outage exception applies to STORED: v0.4.1 text "It is written to the hub record before the call to the sender" holds while the hub is reachable; during an outage it is written to the receiver's hash-chained local log first and replayed on return. [R] (changed in v0.5 by CR-9, B′ ruling 2026-10-08) STORED means durable in the receiver's own store; the hub additionally keeps a bounded encrypted copy of the content (R-80). Until a stage acknowledged during an outage has been replayed, the receiver's disk holds the only copy (RR-15, accepted). [R] (v0.5.1, OQ-5 ruling A, 2026-10-08; GP-13; threat model 12.2) Durability floor of the store. It survives F-1 (the sidecar killed at any instruction) and F-2 (host crash or power loss): the record is written to a temporary name, flushed to stable storage, renamed, and the directory flushed, and STORED MUST NOT be reported before that flush reaches stable storage; a store that cannot flush reports failure, not STORED. It detects and shows, never silently: F-3 disk full (STORED refused visibly), F-4 a corrupt record (checksum and chain link, quarantine, resend by digest), F-5 store lost or an older copy restored (reconciled with the hub record, lost-after-STORED flagged; the hub's bounded encrypted copy is the recovery, R-80). It refuses or detects F-6 a second writer (store lock with the owner's identity) and F-7 an attacker writing the store (detected; prevention is RR-2, R-82). The failure classes are the ruling's; the mechanisms are the threat model's (SI-15, SI-16, SI-22) and step 3 takes them as the durability floor.
