docs/design/interactive-agent-communication-01-requirements.md:1675:13.5.1 Step 3 (security floor and phasing): the rule format and the defaults of the policy model (R-73, CR-19); the list of low-risk classes for the policy route (R-72, CR-18), the first being a dead holder's hand-over with a same-role lease successor (R-74); the initial list of high-impact approval classes (R-76, OQ-14); the reconciliation details of the outage log (R-45.a, CR-1); the phasing of the eleven new requirements R-72..R-82 against the existing P1 items. [R] (v0.5.1) Also from the non-CR rulings: the phasing and price of the move to one isolated operating-system account per agent, including group-based access to shared checkouts (OQ-2, R-82: committed target; the shared user is accepted for now; host root stays a permanent residual); the durability floor of the store (OQ-5, R-15.o: F-1 and F-2 survived with a flush before STORED, F-3 to F-5 detected and shown, F-6 and F-7 refused or detected); and the defence against all fourteen adversaries ADV-1..ADV-14 (OQ-1, 2.3).
docs/design/interactive-agent-communication-01-requirements.md:1676:13.5.2 Step 4 (architect): the build order for confidentiality, pin hub card-signing keys out of band first, then agent-to-agent DM encryption, then project mail, break-glass after the operator key (R-80); the cost of re-wrapping message keys for long histories (R-74); the first-build measurement of each [R~] starting number (14.3), each as an acceptance item of the first build (OQ-9); the hub outage measurement over 30 days that re-checks the credential lifetime (hypothesis H-1; build T-3383); the thresholds of the activity veto and the window H-11 (R-81); the "transcript complete" signal per harness (R-47.a); roster format and enrolment (R-77); the claim mechanism that keeps "never handed over twice" across a crash (R-51.a); key pinning and rotation (R-75); (v0.5.1) the design of the narrow privileged helper that creates per-agent accounts, each creation a human-approved logged Tier 0 act (OQ-2, R-82); the store mechanisms behind the durability floor (OQ-5, SI-15, SI-16, SI-22, R-15.o).
